💾 Program 11 — Binary File Writing and Reading

📌 Description

This program demonstrates how to write structured student records to a binary file and read them back.

It uses binary file streams along with "write()" and "read()" to store and retrieve fixed-size records.

🔑 Concepts Covered

- 💾 Binary file handling
- 📝 Writing binary records
- 📖 Reading binary records
- 🎓 Student structures
- 📦 Fixed-size record storage
- 🔄 "write()" and "read()"

📁 File Created

"students.dat"

🧠 Main C++ Features

"std::ios::binary", "write()", and "read()"
